5348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Meeting notes: [Ecosystem Explorer Project](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QBpFmSR54fGus8q6RraUj0-mEjSoX7S7fdlgsvxZsuk/edit?usp=sharing)  \\n\\n  - [https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml](https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml)  \\n\\n### SIG Security: release signing\\n\\n- Robert proposed enabling GitHub “signature releases” in addition to existing tag signing and GPG signatures of source archives.\\n\\n- Key points:\\n\\n  - GitHub’s source tarball/zip is generated at download time; signing artifacts strengthens trust and mitigates changes over time.\\n\\n  - Double-signing is acceptable and beneficial for OSS Scorecard/compliance.\\n\\n  - Constraint: Artifacts must be uploaded at release time; cannot regenerate later.\\n\\n- Decision: Proceed with enabling signature releases; update release documentation and ensure process discipline.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164)  \\n\\n### KubeCon updates\\n\\n- OpenTelemetry Observatory booth confirmed.\\n\\n- Go SIG will meet at the booth (Tuesday morning, local time; check published schedule).\\n\\n- Plan to cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; reminder will be sent next week.\\n\\n- Community encouraged to stop by the booth and participate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"meet note ecosystem explor project http doc googl com document d 1qbpfmsr54fgus8q6rrauj0 mejsox7s7fdlgsvxzsuk edit usp share http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml sig secur releas sign robert propos enabl github signatur releas in addit to exist tag sign and gpg signatur of sourc archiv key point github s sourc tarbal zip is generat at download time sign artifact strengthen trust and mitig chang over time doubl sign is accept and benefici for os scorecard complianc constraint artifact must be upload at releas time can not regener later decis proceed with enabl signatur releas updat releas document and ensur process disciplin refer http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 kubecon updat opentelemetri observatori booth confirm go sig will meet at the booth tuesday morn local time check publish schedul plan to cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week remind will be sent next week communiti encourag to stop by the booth and particip sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"0032f870da180d9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2787941508749597, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09442317267851381, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7089931, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Can you share more about why you aren't able to migrate to the stats handler?  We [deprecated](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/4534) the interceptors almost 2 years ago, which seems like plenty of time to migrate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-28T20:40:37Z\\n\\nEven if we removed all of our references, references in transitive dependencies still cause compilation errors, and we don’t have control over the timeline at which transitive dependencies remove those code references.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-29T08:35:31Z\\n\\nThat doesn't look like a good reason to me. There will always be unmaintained transitive dependencies that prevent this kind of upgrades.\\n\\nThat's tech debt that needs to be fixed, not kept on our end.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T16:28:55Z\\n\\nThe question is really whether we can rely on otelgrpc to be stable! For now, we are stuck on v0.58.0 because of compilation errors on higher versions introduced by the breaking change. If there is an urgent security patch introduced, we won’t be able to upgrade to it.\\n\\nGenerally, with Golang, we avoid breaking changes aggressively avoid these kinds of things. Does maintaining this interceptor involve significant overhead from the maintainers?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T17:37:26Z\\n\\nPlease do not rely on an unstable package as being stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T17:38:42Z\\n\\nAre there plans to make this package stable? Or are we sticking with [ZeroVer](https://0ver.org/) for the forseeable future?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T18:06:47Z\\n\\n> Are there plans to make this package stable?\\n\\nThere is definitely desire among project contributor to progress this package towards stability. But please understand this is an open-source project. It is driven by a the dedicated effort of engineers who donate their time to working on this. That time is valuable and allocated to many efforts.\\n\\nI'm happy to add the question of stabilization to our weekly SIG meeting happening tomorrow. @nicholasngai I would strongly suggest you attend the meeting tomorrow to discuss your use-case and help motivate allocation of effort for this stabilization. I don't anticipate this stabilization happening within 2025, but I could see us prioritizing it for 2026 if we have community involvement and/or added developer help here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"can you share more about whi you aren t abl to migrat to the stat handler we deprec http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 4534 the interceptor almost 2 year ago which seem like plenti of time to migrat nicholasngai 2025 10 28t20 40 37z even if we remov all of our refer refer in transit depend still caus compil error and we don t have control over the timelin at which transit depend remov those code refer dmathieu 2025 10 29t08 35 31z that doesn t look like a good reason to me there will alway be unmaintain transit depend that prevent this kind of upgrad that s tech debt that need to be fix not kept on our end nicholasngai 2025 10 